review_text:
Played the first three on the PS2 and the fourth on the PS4.
Im happy to have a copy in my Steam library too.

but honestly Im just making this review to say please remake and/or port the IMOQ games to Steam too. ^^;

Minor Spoilers!
Pros;
       Nostalgia, Rengeki, Awakening, scenery, great soundtrack, great voice actors(mostly), interesting characters, affection system, customizable weapons, classic jrpg feel. 
Cons;
       Somewhat repetitive, leveling is too easy, level scaling damage makes enemies a few levels lower than you seem pathetically weak, Volume 4 takes about 20 minutes to complete and was a total waste of time, plus the animated cut scenes in volume 4 do not play well, not to mention Haseos 5th form takes over and makes your previous skills and weapons unusable.

With all of this in mind, I would still recommend this game to any anime, or classic rpg fans out there. Its still alot of fun, and the story is wild. Especially recommended to any sword art fans out there since this is a remake of the game/anime that sword art ripped off.
